    "result_text": "The exploration report confirms my implementation matches the codebase conventions exactly \u2014 and it independently arrived at the same design I already implemented and verified (new checked exception + handler + escalation YAML + a `Check` step wired into the pipeline).\n\nNo further action is needed. The work is complete and verified:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerEmailDomain`** rejects blocklisted domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 throws `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n- Handler maps it to **400** via the shared `ProblemDetails.build` helper, wired through the escalation YAML.\n- Wired into **both** `owners.POST.yml` (after `BuildOwner`) and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (after `ApplyOwner`) \u2014 which covers the create/update asymmetry the report flagged (update doesn't go through `BuildOwner`'s email validation).\n\nThe report's coverage caveat (JaCoCo 85%/66%) is satisfied: the acceptance test drives the mailinator path end-to-end, exercising the check function, the exception constructor, and the handler. `./mvnw -o test` reported **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
